                "retweet_count": 30,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "In New Jersey, a Black woman is almost 7 times more likely to die from maternity-related complications than a white woman. Black babies are more than 3 times more likely to die before their first birthday than white babies.\n\nIn a state with some of the best hospitals in the country, that\u2019s unacceptable. As governor, I\u2019ll double down on the good work of Nurture NJ and the Maternal and Infant Health Innovation Authority and work to address racial bias in our health care system, diversify our perinatal workforce, and improve health outcomes for Black women in NJ. #BlackMaternalHealthWeek",
